---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
        title="Legal — CivicBrands"
        description="Legal information for CivicBrands."
>
    <section class="section">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>

        <div class="measure">
            <h1>Legal</h1>

            <p>
                CivicBrands is a public DBA of BJL13 Enterprise Solutions LLC. This page collects legal notices and organizational legal context for the CivicBrands public website.
            </p>

            <p>
                The site is maintained as an informational and publication surface. Published materials may include research, records, memoranda, and representative work summaries.
            </p>

            <h2>Good-faith interpretation</h2>
            <p>
                CivicBrands tries to write public terms in language people can actually understand.
                If a notice is ambiguous, the intended reading is the one that preserves informed use,
                accessibility, and repair over technical advantage.
            </p>

            <h2>No professional advice</h2>
            <p>
                The site may discuss public records, agencies, benefits, courts, health systems, housing,
                or emergency services. That material is information, not legal, medical, financial, or
                professional advice. Decisions with legal, medical, safety, or financial consequences
                should be checked with the appropriate qualified person or primary source.
            </p>

            <h2>Emergency limits</h2>
            <p>
                CivicBrands does not provide emergency services. If you are in immediate danger, call
                911 or the relevant local emergency number. Crisis and resource pages are built to help
                people find routes, not to replace responders, clinicians, advocates, or direct service
                providers.
            </p>

            <h2>External sources</h2>
            <p>
                Links to agencies, service providers, repositories, public records, and third-party sites
                are provided for context and access. A link does not mean endorsement, control, or a
                promise that the outside page will remain accurate.
            </p>

            <h2>Corrections</h2>
            <p>
                If something here is materially wrong, tell us. For KC directory corrections, use
                <a href="/kc/suggest">Suggest / correct</a>. For other pages, email
                <a href="mailto:contact@mail.civicbrands.org">contact@mail.civicbrands.org</a>. The goal is repair
                of the public record, not defense of an error.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
